# engram

Hooks store prompts, replies, and tool calls automatically (verbatim, no
summarization, no LLM). The Python package is still `lore`; MCP tools stay
`memory_recall` / `memory_observe`.

- If hook context is missing at the start of a turn, call `memory_recall`
  with the user's wording before acting.
- Store new facts and tool results with `memory_observe`. Never summarize
  or distill into memory — pass text as-is.
- Namespace is inferred from the project (`CURSOR_PROJECT_DIR` / git / cwd).
  Do not invent a different namespace unless the user asks.
- Hooks skip MCP tools whose names start with `memory_` to avoid recursion.
- Home dir is `~/.lore` (`LORE_HOME`, or `ENGRAM_HOME` as an alias).
